- ssim2_delta_avg = +0.0017

## Why ship as opt-in, not default

The 6 SCREEN cells regression (graph d=6 -0.99 SSIM2, windows d=4
-0.32, imessage d=6 -0.37) would cause FIXED → OPEN flips on the
cjxl_parity_ledger. The W44-65/W44-68 gate currently protects these
cells by also dropping `try_dct32`.

A per-image discriminator using zenanalyze proxies separates codec_wiki
from the regressing screens cleanly:

| image       | m3_colour | edge_density | fcbr  | benefit_keep? |
|---          |---        |---           |---    |---            |
| codec_wiki  | **143.66**| **0.039**    | 0.904 | YES           |
| imessage    | 67.65     | 0.053        | 0.832 | borderline    |
| graph       | 11.75     | 0.070        | 0.809 | NO            |
| windows     | 20.69     | 0.119        | 0.769 | NO            |
| imac_g3     | 14.31     | 0.122        | 0.774 | borderline    |
| terminal    | 13.52     | 0.087        | 0.833 | YES (preserved) |

`m3_colourfulness > 60` AND `edge_density < 0.05` would cleanly
admit codec_wiki only. Default-on with this auto-gate is a future
chunk; this commit ships the opt-in surface so callers with
zenanalyze classifiers can already wire it.

## Decoder validation

Verified on `/tmp/w44_123_codec_wiki_e{5,6,7}_keep.jxl` via:
- jxl-rs: header parse + basic_info → OK on all 3 cells
- jxl-oxide: full `render_frame(0)` with srgb_linear → OK on all 3 cells
- djxl v0.12.0 (libjxl d2c7032): decoded to PNG, 245 / 240 / 213 MP/s
  on the 2560×1664 image, 32 threads.

